=== ebtables ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ebtables 1.8.10 (nf_tables)


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  ebtables -[ADI] chain rule-specification [options]
  ebtables -P chain target
  ebtables -[LFZ] [chain]
  ebtables -[NX] [chain]
  ebtables -E old-chain-name new-chain-name


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  chain


FLAGS (25) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-A, --append chain            append to chain
-D, --delete chain            delete matching rule from chain
-D, --delete chain rulenum    delete rule at position rulenum from chain
-C, --change-counters chain [rulenum] pcnt bcnt change counters of existing
                              rule
-I, --insert chain rulenum    insert rule at position rulenum in chain
-L, --list [chain]            list the rules in a chain or in all chains
-F, --flush [chain]           delete all rules in chain or in all chains
    --init-table              replace the kernel table with the initial
                              table
-Z, --zero [chain]            put counters on zero in chain or in all chains
-P, --policy chain target     change policy on chain to target
-N, --new-chain chain         create a user defined chain
-E, --rename-chain old new    rename a chain
-X, --delete-chain [chain]    delete a user defined chain

Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
[!] -p, --proto proto         protocol hexadecimal, by name or LENGTH
[!] -s, --src address[/mask]  source mac address
[!] -d, --dst address[/mask]  destination mac address
[!] -i, --in-if name[+]       network input interface name
[!] -o, --out-if name[+]      network output interface name
    [!] --logical-in name[+]  logical bridge input interface name
    [!] --logical-out name[+] logical bridge output interface name
-c, --set-counters chain pcnt bcnt set the counters of the to be added rule
-M, --modprobe program        try to insert modules using this program
    --concurrent              use a file lock to support concurrent scripts
-v, --verbose                 verbose mode
-V, --version                 print package version
